From: mixelpixx <11727006+mixelpixx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: mesh shaders as compute without VK_EXT_mesh_shader

Hosts without VK_EXT_mesh_shader, such as the PS4's GCN2 GPU under RADV,
could not run games that draw with mesh shaders. There the recompiler
emits the mesh program as a compute shader that writes its vertices and
triangle indices to the GPU-only utility buffer, and a generated vertex
shader draws them with an indexed draw. KYTY_MESH_COMPUTE=1 forces this
path on hosts that have the extension.

Indirect mesh draws read their records on the CPU in this mode, and Layer
is chosen per vertex rather than per primitive.
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -731,6 +731,11 @@ if(BUILD_TESTING)
 		COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:shader_recompiler_compute_tests> --alignbyte-only)
 	add_test(NAME graphics_pipeline_rasterization
 		COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:shader_recompiler_compute_tests> --polygon-mode-only)
+	# The same draws with mesh shaders run as compute, as on hosts without VK_EXT_mesh_shader.
+	add_test(NAME graphics_pipeline_rasterization_mesh_compute
+		COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:shader_recompiler_compute_tests> --polygon-mode-only)
+	set_tests_properties(graphics_pipeline_rasterization_mesh_compute
+		PROPERTIES ENVIRONMENT KYTY_MESH_COMPUTE=1)
 	add_test(NAME graphics_draw_offsets
 		COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:shader_recompiler_compute_tests> --draw-offset-only)
 	add_test(NAME virtual_memory_allocation
